  "Question": "For real numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y,\\) define \\(x \\spadesuit y = (x+y)(x-y).\\) What is \\(3 \\spadesuit (4 \\spadesuit 5)?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-72\\)",
    "B": "\\(-27\\)",
    "C": "\\(-24\\)",
    "D": "\\(24\\)",
    "E": "\\(72\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The parentheses tell us to evaluate \\(4\\spadesuit5\\) first. Substituting into the given rule gives\n\\[\n4\\spadesuit5=(4+5)(4-5)=9(-1)=-9.\n\\]\nNow use \\(-9\\) as the second input of the outer operation:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n3\\spadesuit(-9)\n&=(3+(-9))(3-(-9))\\\\\n&=(-6)(12)=-72.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThus the value is \\(\\boxed{-72}\\), choice A.",
